{"title":"Subset Sum Problem","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given an array of `n` positive integers and a target value `target`. Decide whether some subset of the array (any selection of elements, each element used at most once) adds up to exactly `target`.\n\nElements are distinguished by position, so equal values at different positions count as different elements. The empty subset has sum `0`, but `target` is always at least `1`.","inputFormat":"The first line contains two integers `n` and `target`.\nThe second line contains `n` integers: the array.","outputFormat":"Print `YES` if some subset sums to `target`, otherwise print `NO`.","constraints":["1 ≤ n ≤ 300","1 ≤ nums[i] ≤ 10^4","1 ≤ target ≤ 10^4"],"examples":[{"input":"4 14\n7 3 9 4","output":"YES","explanation":"7 + 3 + 4 = 14."},{"input":"4 15\n7 3 9 4","output":"NO","explanation":"The subset sums of this array are 0, 3, 4, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 19, 20 and 23. The value 15 is not among them."}],"tests":[{"input":"1 5\n5","output":"YES"},{"input":"1 5\n6","output":"NO"},{"input":"1 1\n1","output":"YES"},{"input":"3 10\n3 3 3","output":"NO"},{"input":"3 9\n3 3 3","output":"YES"},{"input":"3 100\n1 2 3","output":"NO"},{"input":"1 10000\n10000","output":"YES"},{"input":"3 9999\n10000 10000 10000","output":"NO"},{"input":"2 7\n15 11","output":"NO"},{"input":"2 21\n16 2","output":"NO"},{"input":"3 2\n16 3 5","output":"NO"},{"input":"3 5\n11 17 7","output":"NO"},{"input":"4 15\n8 14 3 18","output":"NO"},{"input":"4 3\n17 7 5 2","output":"NO"},{"input":"5 18\n6 4 9 15 14","output":"YES"},{"input":"5 6\n7 15 3 11 7","output":"NO"},{"input":"6 28\n19 19 2 17 7 15","output":"YES"},{"input":"6 18\n15 11 6 10 19 20","output":"NO"},{"input":"300 9999\n5376 6562 3710 9838 3078 6718 7456 6298 5190 2110 7056 6802 4566 4138 1738 5786 6562 4536 1560 6970 7628 8488 8868 9180 7506 264 9744 8762 5104 1220 22 9042 1368 7468 5318 5196 5320 7012 6292 9512 6772 5634 8436 6266 9006 3832 5354 8930 3692 1550 684 12